Chapter: BvtFoodSweep
  cites Uoaix chapter CompositeGameRules
  cites Uoaix chapter CompositeProduction
  cites Uoaix chapter BvtCheck

 Every economy food (ep-food, items 1 to 200) is made or harvested as an art that eats (cg-food-fill above 0); the text
 names any item that is not, with its art.
  bfs-sweep : Integer, Text -> Text
  bfs-sweep (item) (out) = if item > 200 then out
    else if not (ep-food item) then bfs-sweep (item + 1) out
    else let made = cpr-material-art item
    in let art = if made /= 0 then made else gh-output-graphic item
    in bfs-sweep (item + 1) (if art /= 0 & cg-food-fill art > 0 then out else out & " " & show item & "@" & show art)
  bvt-food-sweep : Integer -> [Console] Integer
  bvt-food-sweep (unused) = act
    missing <- bfs-sweep 1 ""
    a <- bvt-check ("every economy food's made art eats; missing:" & missing) (missing == "")
    b <- bvt-check "both bread loaf arts eat (0x103B listed, 0x103C by the catalog), and a bag (0x0E76) does not" (cg-food-fill #103B > 0 & cg-food-fill #103C > 0 & cg-food-fill #0E76 == 0)
    a + b
  end
